For the newer readers in the group, a "glasses" thresad starts up
every couple of months.  The "just kidding" was an indication that
I didn't feel like bringing up the subject again.  Tha is, until
I though up the following pun:

Mirrored sunglasses, gives you the "reflection" attribute, also known
as "Ray Ban"'s (get it?).

So, to beat the subject to death,
 here's a list of possible glasses:
1) mirrored glasses (as above)
	Causes confusion if you (a)pply a mirror to yourself while
	wearing these.
2) rhinestone shades (act as hawaiian shirt)
3) cheap sun glasses:  basic protection from blinding flashes (yellow
	lights, lightning).
4) really,really dark glasses (+'s to charisma)
	makes all rooms "dark" while wearing.  Protection from some
	gaze attacks (like Umberhulks),
	since the monster can't make "eye contact"
5) Peril sensitive glasses (ala Hitchhiker's Guide)
	Blind you whenever a hostile monster in an adjacent square.
	On the good side, monsters will think you are invisible
	(read the books).
6) Reading glasses
	Increase chance of succesfully reading a spellbook.
	Bonus when searching and engraving.
7) X-ray vision glasses
	Reveal (i.e. map) all spaces in a straight line from where
	you are in one of the 8 directions.  Small chance of
	polymorphing due to all the radiation.  A tedious form of
	mapping, but good for finding treasure vaults and seeing
	what's behind the boulder.
8) The evil nazi hypno-monocle
	charms/tames creatures when applied.
9) IR goggles
	All rooms are treated as if they were lit.  Worth wishing
	for if you hate dark rooms.
10) The "rear view mirror" glasses advertised on TV
	Negates suprise from monster that sneak up on you. (acts
	like searching for some creatures (do jaguars have the
	ability to suprise you?)).
11) safety glasses
	Yet another way to add to your armor class.
12) airline eye-cover  (yeah, I'm out of good ideas)
	A blindfold of restful sleep.
13) magnifying glasses
	good for frying ants (ok, I'll stop now).

You see the Medusa.
She's so ugly your lenses crack!  Luckily it happened before
you got a good look at her. (glasses now act as a blindfold).

The nymph smiles nervously, unable to make eye contact.

You inspect the chest for traps.
You see some fine print not visible to the naked eye.
It says "Made in Hell"

Quaffing from a fountain:
Water sprays in your face!  Your glasses fog up!

And of course we'll need the Keystone Motorcycle Kop with
mirrored glasses and scrolls of punishment.

